ICCV-2025-P0213,ICCV-2025-A001247,Hanxiao Jiang,shared,3,6,6,"University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign Teleoperation Digital Twin Overlay Model-Based Robot Planning Left Hand Real-Time Physical Simulation & Rendering Right Hand t Input Video PhysTwin Simulation Applications in Robotics Figure . PhysTwin takes sparse videos (three camera views) of deformable objects under interaction as input and reconstructs a simulatable digital twin with complete geometry, high-fidelity appearance, and accurate physical parameters. This enables multiple applications, such as real-time interactive simulation using keyboards and robotic teleoperation devices, as well as model-based robot planning. . Introduction",-2,data/raw/iccv/2025/first_pages/ICCV-2025-P0213.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/ICCV2025/papers/Jiang_PhysTwin_Physics-Informed_Reconstruction_and_Simulation_of_Deformable_Objects_from_Videos_ICCV_2025_paper.pdf
