ICCV-2025-P0500,ICCV-2025-A002895,Anh Thai,shared,3,5,5,"Google DeepMind Work done as a student researcher at Google DeepMind. Visual-Language Feature Maps 3D-Language Gaussian Field Pretrained Multimodal image encoder Projector from 2D VLM ⋮ Feed-forward 3D-Language Gaussian Splatting Model Text prompt: “What is next to the bed?” Large Langue Model Self-supervised 3D-Language Gaussian Splatting Training Text response: “The desk” Downstream Task: 3D VQA Figure . SplatTalk. We propose a self-supervised 3D-Language Gaussian Splatting model trained from multi-view RGB images. First, images are encoded using a pretrained 2D Vision-Language Model (VLM) and projected into visual-language feature maps via a multimodal projector. These feature maps are then learned within a feed-forward 3D-Language Gaussian Splatting model, producing a 3D-Language Gaussian Field that encodes spatial and semantic information in 3D space. During inference, the 3D Gaussian features are directly queried by a Large Language Model (LLM) to perform 3D question-answering (3D VQA) tasks. . Introduction",-2,data/raw/iccv/2025/first_pages/ICCV-2025-P0500.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/ICCV2025/papers/Thai_SplatTalk_3D_VQA_with_Gaussian_Splatting_ICCV_2025_paper.pdf
