ICCV-2025-P0971,ICCV-2025-A005670,Delong Zhang,shared,3,7,7,"School of Computer Science and Engineering, Sun Yat-sen University, China; Shopee; Key Laboratory of Machine Intelligence and Advanced Computing, Ministry of Education, China. Target Person Garment Ours StableVITON D4-VTON GP-VTON Warped Garment Figure . Warping-based method (e.g. GP-VTON) is prone to severe visual artifacts and distortions (see the green dashed box) affected by the incorrect prediction of warp module. Learning-based methods (e.g. StableVTON and D4 -VTON) are difﬁcult to reconstruct complex detailed textures (see the red dashed box). Our FIA-VTON designs a Flow Infused Attention module, utilizing the warping ﬂow as an implicit guidance to reconstruct complex detailed textures while maintaining the consistency of the garment.",-11,data/raw/iccv/2025/first_pages/ICCV-2025-P0971.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/ICCV2025/papers/Zhang_Learning_Implicit_Features_with_Flow-Infused_Transformations_for_Realistic_Virtual_Try-On_ICCV_2025_paper.pdf
