ICCV-2025-P1136,ICCV-2025-A006668,Xin Wen,shared,3,5,5,"University of Hong Kong Equal Contribution Project Lead University of Edinburgh Corresponding Author Huawei London Research Centre Imperial College London Figure . Image reconstruction using our structured visual tokenization approach, which uniquely enables decoding at any token count. Each column shows reconstructions resulting from progressively increasing the number of tokens, from a single token to tokens. Unlike conventional tokenizers that require a fixed number of tokens for meaningful decoding, our method ensures that each token incrementally refines the image, with earlier tokens capturing the most salient features and later ones adding finer details. This demonstrates the flexibility and effectiveness of our approach in producing coherent images even with very few tokens (view more from Fig. in the Appendix).",-1,data/raw/iccv/2025/first_pages/ICCV-2025-P1136.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/ICCV2025/papers/Wen_Principal_Components_Enable_A_New_Language_of_Images_ICCV_2025_paper.pdf
