ICCV-2025-P1214,ICCV-2025-A007148,Jiwen Yu,shared,3,6,6,"Kuaishou Technology W W A S D A Space S W D Space A S W D A Space S W D A Space W S D Space A S D A S Space ( ) Prompt: Standing in the cherry blossom forest with a gun in first person perspective. W A S W D A Space S W W D A Space S D A Space S W W D Space A S D Space D Space ( ) Prompt: An emerald green velvet accent chair sits prominently in the center of a minimalist room. W W A S D Space A W S D Space A S Space A S W W W D D Space A S D Space A S A S D Space D Space ( ) Prompt: A large Saint Bernard walks steadily across the vast, snow-covered expanse of a mountain range. W A S Space A S W W W D D Space A S D A Space S W D Space A S W D Space ( ) Prompt: In a Renaissance palace, from a first person perspective, one can see a lion in front. Figure . We propose GameFactory, a framework that leverages the powerful generative capabilities of pre-trained video models for the creation of new games. By learning action control from a small-scale first-person Minecraft dataset, this framework can transfer these control abilities to open-domain videos, ultimately allowing the creation of new games within open-domain scenes. As illustrated in ( )( ), GameFactory supports action control across diverse, newly generated scenes in open domains, paving the way for the development of entirely new game experiences. The yellow buttons indicate pressed keys, and the arrows represent the direction of mouse movements.",-4,data/raw/iccv/2025/first_pages/ICCV-2025-P1214.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/ICCV2025/papers/Yu_GameFactory_Creating_New_Games_with_Generative_Interactive_Videos_ICCV_2025_paper.pdf
