ICCV-2025-P1387,ICCV-2025-A008162,Jiawei He,shared,3,10,10,"Beijing Academy of Artificial Intelligence, Galbot, Tsinghua University, Peking University, Institute of Automation, Chinese Academy of Sciences, Shanghai Jiao Tong University, Eastern Institute of Technology Project Page: Grasp the metal head of the hammer Grasp the handle of the hammer Grasp the body of the cup Grasp the handle of the cup Figure . Overview. Our main contributions are twofold: First, we constructed a large-scale synthetic dexterous grasping dataset called DexGraspNet3. , which contains grasp poses with captions describing the grasped part and style. Second, we trained a language-instructed grasp pose prediction model using the DexGraspNet3. dataset, called DexVLG. This model can generate language-aligned and generalizable grasping poses for different objects in real-world experiments.",-3,data/raw/iccv/2025/first_pages/ICCV-2025-P1387.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/ICCV2025/papers/He_DexVLG_Dexterous_Vision-Language-Grasp_Model_at_Scale_ICCV_2025_paper.pdf
