ICCV-2025-P1624,ICCV-2025-A009575,Wenjia Wang,shared,3,10,10,"Shanghai AI Laboratory . Carry a heavy luggage . Pickup luggage . Side-lie sadly . Walk drunkenly . Tired and rest Agent: Sure, I found it is suitable to use style sad, tired and drunk from our script database. Agent: I have retrieved the top-k samples from our sad, tired and drunk database. . Sad and cry Agent: I am now generating long-term scripts based on Retrieval-Augmented Generation. Here are the final retrieved keyframes and I will parse them into condition labels and feed them into the Finite State Machine to drive the humanoid: . Drink a wine . Idle drunkenly . Put luggage on table Figure . SIMS enables physically simulated characters to perform diverse skills within complex 3D scenes given long-term daily narratives and scene inputs. Our character could perform versatile skills, including Locomotions, Human Scene Interactions and Dynamic Object Interactions with diverse styles while accomplishing physically plausible contacts and obstacle avoidance. Left: a dialogue-based retrievalaugmented script generation process. Right: a skillful humanoid performing diverse stylized interactions in a 3D scene.",0,data/raw/iccv/2025/first_pages/ICCV-2025-P1624.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/ICCV2025/papers/Wang_SIMS_Simulating_Stylized_Human-Scene_Interactions_with_Retrieval-Augmented_Script_Generation_ICCV_2025_paper.pdf
