ICCV-2025-P1779,ICCV-2025-A010504,Yuang Wang,shared,3,8,8,"Input Image Visual Action Prompts Generated Scene Dynamics Figure . We propose visual action prompts as unified representations for complex, high-degree-of-freedom actions (e.g., simulating scene dynamics driven by human hands or robotic grippers). Visual action prompts are “renderings” of subjects’ action-induced 3D strucutres, among which we use skeleton as the primary representaion for its acquisition efficiency. This paradigm enables training action-driven video generation models across heterogeneous datasets while facilitating cross-domain knowledge transfer.",-6,data/raw/iccv/2025/first_pages/ICCV-2025-P1779.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/ICCV2025/papers/Wang_Precise_Action-to-Video_Generation_Through_Visual_Action_Prompts_ICCV_2025_paper.pdf
