ICCV-2025-P1863,ICCV-2025-A010996,Fatemeh Ghezloo,shared,3,9,9,"University of Washington Microsoft University of California, Los Angeles Allen Institute for AI (AI2) Figure . We propose PathFinder, a system capable of navigating image patches in a whole slide image, describe each patch to collect evidence, and produce a diagnosis. Pathfinder’s process is interpretable and reminiscent of pathologists. Our system consists of multiple steps carried out by multi-modal agents: ) Initial Assessment by Triage Agent; ) Evidence Collection by Navigation and Description Agents; and ) Integrated Diagnosis by Diagnosis Agent.",-5,data/raw/iccv/2025/first_pages/ICCV-2025-P1863.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/ICCV2025/papers/Ghezloo_PathFinder_A_Multi-Modal_Multi-Agent_System_for_Medical_Diagnostic_Decision-Making_Applied_ICCV_2025_paper.pdf
