ICCV-2025-P2287,ICCV-2025-A013513,Ziyang Luo,shared,3,8,8,"Northwestern Polytechnical University Mohamed bin Zayed University of Artificial Intelligence Institute of Artificial Intelligence, Hefei Comprehensive National Science Center (a) Previous Model Baby laughing (b) TAViS Audio foundation model Class Name or Visual foundation model Baby playing with dog Audio Input Frames Baby babbling Project to common space Baby chasing dog Segmentation Baby playing with dog Segmentation Baby climbing Segmentation GroundTruth w/o text bridged w/ text bridged Text Space Segmentation Visual foundation model Image (c) Comparison results Baby Baby laughing Baby ImageBind Baby crying Audio1 ImageBind Audio2 off-the-shelf combine Audio Space Prompt Visual Space SAM2 Figure . Illustration of TAViS compared with previous methods. ( ) Previous methods often rely on single-modality foundation models (top) or combine the visual foundation model with ImageBind in an off-the-shelf manner (bottom), which limits their ability to address the misalignment of audio-visual information with significant intra-class diversity. ( ) We propose TAViS, a novel framework that leverages two foundation models: ImageBind and SAM2. The text-bridged alignment between visual and audio modalities serves as both prompts and supervision signals for TAViS. ( ) We demonstrate the effectiveness of our approach through comparative experiments with and without the text-bridged mechanism.",-5,data/raw/iccv/2025/first_pages/ICCV-2025-P2287.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/ICCV2025/papers/Luo_TAViS_Text-bridged_Audio-Visual_Segmentation_with_Foundation_Models_ICCV_2025_paper.pdf
