ICCV-2025-P2395,ICCV-2025-A014189,Yicheng Feng,shared,3,7,7,"School of Computer Science, Peking University, University of California, San Diego, Renmin University of China, BeingBeyond Object-level Details token token … Pooling Q: What activity does the video depict? VideoLLaMA2. : The video shows a person riding a three-wheeled scooter. VideoOrion: The video depicts a person using a red three-wheeled scooter to clean the floor by attaching a mop to it. Concat … Action-level Details Q-Former Q: What activity does the video depict? VideoLLaMA2. : The video shows a woman performing a diving routine. VideoOrion: The video depicts a woman in a black swimsuit performing a backflip off a diving board into a pool. (a) VideoOrion capturing more details … Ours (b) Performance on finer details and object tasks (c) Entangled v.s. disentangled visual representation Figure . With explicit modeling of object dynamics, VideoOrion can (a) grasp finer details (b) with understanding on object-related finegrained details. (c) Comparison with prior encoding including: ( ) spatial pooling the whole frame into a single token; ( ) concatenating adjacent patch tokens into a single token; ( ) Q-Former aggregates patch tokens with learnable queries. ( ) VideoOrion with object tokens providing disentangled semantics. tics, VideoOrion not only offers a more natural and efficient way to derive compact, disentangled semantic representations but also enables explicit object modeling of video content with minimal computational cost. Moreover, the introduced object tokens naturally allow VideoOrion to accomplish video-based referring tasks. Experimental results show that VideoOrion can learn to make good use of the object tokens, and achieves competitive results on both general video question answering and video-based referring benchmarks.",-15,data/raw/iccv/2025/first_pages/ICCV-2025-P2395.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/ICCV2025/papers/Feng_VideoOrion_Tokenizing_Object_Dynamics_in_Videos_ICCV_2025_paper.pdf
