ICCV-2025-P2518,ICCV-2025-A014932,Guangzhao He,shared,3,5,5,"Zhejiang University . TCSR . NICP ATE3D . . SuperGraph (Ours) . NSFP NDP . . ERNet (Ours) Neural Deformation FPS Pyramids (a) ERNet Registered Trajectories (b) Comparison Results on D-FAUST (a) SuperGraph Registered Correspondence (b) Registration Quailty Comparison Figure . (a) Given a source object (center bunny) and a sequence of sparse or partial point clouds (purple bunnies), ERNet efficiently and accurately predicts feed-forward registrations. The gradient texture on the center bunny corresponds to the colors of its vertex-wise trajectories shown above. (b) ERNet achieves the lowest Average Trajectory Error in 3D (AT E3D ) among all baselines on the D-FAUST dataset while delivering over 4x speedup in FPS.",-14,data/raw/iccv/2025/first_pages/ICCV-2025-P2518.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/ICCV2025/papers/He_ERNet_Efficient_Non-Rigid_Registration_Network_for_Point_Sequences_ICCV_2025_paper.pdf
