ICCV-2025-P2655,ICCV-2025-A015731,Zexi Jia,shared,3,9,9,"WeChat AI, Tencent Inc, China Institute for Artificial Intelligence, Peking University (b) Counterfactual Sets (a) Negative Captions Pairs Black dog on the right of yellow cat. Black dog on the right of yellow cat. Yellow dog on the right of black cat. Adding a non-existent object Black car on the right of yellow tree. (c) Case Study The man is to the right of the door Positive Pair CLIP-Similarity Ours . . The door is to the right of the man . . The crouched man and the open floor . . The open man and the crouched floor . . The man is on the train car . . The train car is on the man . . Easy Negative Pair A yellow cat with wide-open eyes is on the left of a black dog with tilted head and curled ears, and a beautiful white cat with smile is on the right of the black dog. Modifying an existing object A black cat on the left of a black dog. The cat has striking yellow eyes and a sleek, shiny coat, while the dog has a similar shiny black coat and expressive brown eyes. Deleting an existing object A yellow cat sitting on green lawn. The cat has a calm and attentive expression, with its ears perked up and its tail slightly curled. Counterfactual Pair (Hard Negative) Paired Caption Modifying Caption Figure . Our Generation of Counterfactual Sets (GCS) strategy differs significantly from traditional methods (a) that rely solely on surfacelevel textual changes. We introduce an innovative data synthesis strategy that combines real-world image-caption pairs with generative models. Specifically, we construct counterfactual datasets (b) by recomposing the puzzle pieces within images: i) adding elements, ii) modifying elements, and iii) removing elements. Additionally, we use a large language model (LLM) to generate detailed aligned captions and develop a new, efficient loss function specifically designed for counterfactual datasets. (c) Our model demonstrates higher accuracy and stronger confidence in selecting the correct caption from two given options.",-15,data/raw/iccv/2025/first_pages/ICCV-2025-P2655.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/ICCV2025/papers/Jia_A_Visual_Leap_in_CLIP_Compositionality_Reasoning_through_Generation_of_ICCV_2025_paper.pdf
